    "reading": "A community recycling facility handles plastic bottles in several distinct stages. First, bottles are collected from public containers and taken to a sorting centre. Workers and automated equipment remove unsuitable materials. The remaining bottles are washed to remove labels and residue before they are crushed into small pieces. These pieces are processed into pellets that may be used in manufacturing new items. Throughout the system, quality checks help prevent contamination. A process description should present the sequence clearly and avoid unsupported commentary about cost or environmental benefits. The writer should also distinguish stages that happen in order from steps that may take place at the same time.",
